===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Tormented by [[witch]]es, [[demon]]s, or evil [[spirit]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1888|year_published=|author={{w|Rudyard Kipling}}|title={{w|The Phantom 'Rickshaw and Other Tales}}|chapter=The Phantom Rickshaw|location=Allahabad|publisher=A.H. Wheeler and Co.|page=9|text=Two months afterwards he was reported fit for duty, but, in spite of the fact that he was urgently needed to help an undermanned Commission stagger through a deficit, he preferred to die; vowing at the last that he was '''hag-ridden'''.}}
# [[torment|Torment]]ed, [[harass]]ed or [[worried]].
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/1906/03/anatole-france/637947/|title=Anatole France|year=1906|month=March|author=Bradford Torrey|work=The Atlantic|passage=So Sir Walter Scott, '''hag-ridden''' by debt, if he finished a novel in the morning began another in the afternoon, because, as he explained, it was less difficult to keep the machine running than to start it again after a rest.}}
# [[overburden|Overburden]]ed by [[fear]] or [[dread]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1942|title=The {{w|Screwtape Letters}}|author=w:C. S. Lewis|text=a man '''hagridden''' by the future, haunted by visions of an imminent heaven or hell upon earth}}

